00:14:01,823 --> 00:14:05,823
Yeah, everybody was. In fact, the whole movie was amazing.

262
00:14:05,823 --> 00:14:09,823
Hey, Coboteau! Did you hear? Your haughty big brother thought you were amazing!

263
00:14:09,823 --> 00:14:16,823
I totally agree, Coboteau. You blew my mind! I thought you were the best thing about it!

264
00:14:20,823 --> 00:14:25,823
Uh, sorry. It looks like our diva just needed a moment.

265
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:26,823
No worries.

266
00:14:26,823 --> 00:14:31,823
So, uh, is Coboteau popular here or something? I'm a little freaked out right now.

267
00:14:31,823 --> 00:14:34,823
Yeah! Duh! And it's more than just our class.

268
00:14:34,823 --> 00:14:36,823
The whole school worship's room wants to be your friend.

269
00:14:36,823 --> 00:14:38,823
I had no idea.

270
00:14:38,823 --> 00:14:39,823
Except...

271
00:14:39,823 --> 00:14:40,823
Hmm?

272
00:14:40,823 --> 00:14:44,823
Well, I don't know if that actually makes her popular since she doesn't want to talk to anybody.

273
00:14:44,823 --> 00:14:47,823
I kinda don't think she likes people very much.

274
00:14:47,823 --> 00:14:50,823
Okay, I shouldn't say people, I guess. Just not us.

275
00:14:50,823 --> 00:14:52,823
Hmm. Very interesting.

276
00:14:52,823 --> 00:14:56,823
We're always telling her how much we adore her, but it's like the more we try to get close to her,

277
00:14:56,823 --> 00:14:59,823
the more she pulls away or maybe she just doesn't take us seriously.

278
00:14:59,823 --> 00:15:04,823
Oh my gosh, please don't hate my guts. I'm not trying to badmouth your sister. I love her.

279
00:15:04,823 --> 00:15:07,823
I'm really a fan of her awkwardness. It's like totes endearing.

280
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:09,823
See you later.

281
00:15:09,823 --> 00:15:13,823
Doesn't take compliments. Pulls away when you try to get close.

282
00:15:13,823 --> 00:15:16,823
Sure sounds like that runs in the family.

283
00:15:16,823 --> 00:15:18,823
Huh? Sorry, what did you say?

284
00:15:18,823 --> 00:15:24,823
What's wrong, Maria?

285
00:15:24,823 --> 00:15:28,823
I'm bored. I wanna go home and stuff my face.

286
00:15:28,823 --> 00:15:38,823
Huh?

287
00:15:38,823 --> 00:15:39,823
Huh?

288
00:15:39,823 --> 00:15:40,823
Coo-coo-coo.

289
00:15:40,823 --> 00:15:43,823
Dry your mortal eyes. You shall wait for me no longer.

290
00:15:43,823 --> 00:15:47,823
Ah! The smelly vampire has returned and we can kill her once and for all!

291
00:15:47,823 --> 00:15:50,823
Do we stone her? Drown her? How are we gonna do it?

292
00:15:50,823 --> 00:15:56,823
Your idiocy amuses me to no end, minion of God. Someday you will look great.

293
00:15:56,823 --> 00:15:57,823
Ah!

294
00:15:57,823 --> 00:16:00,823
Oh, why do you keep jumping at me like that? Are you trying to get me to destroy you?

295
00:16:00,823 --> 00:16:03,823
Are you trying to get me to destroy you? I can smell the crazy leafy out of you.

296
00:16:03,823 --> 00:16:06,823
I have powers that would have your God on his knees begging me for lessons.

297
00:16:06,823 --> 00:16:12,823
Okay, let's get moving. We can film Kobito's scene next since she's already warmed up.

298
00:16:12,823 --> 00:16:14,823
I didn't even know Kobito was in this.

299
00:16:14,823 --> 00:16:19,823
Yeah, of course she is. I realize this might make it a little awkward for you because we've decided to have her do all your secrets.

300
00:16:19,823 --> 00:16:22,823
Is she replacing me or was I just a stand-in for her all along?

301
00:16:22,823 --> 00:16:26,823
Look at that sunset. It's the perfect location for our next shot. Let's go!

302
00:16:26,823 --> 00:16:28,823
We're on it. You can count on us.

303
00:16:28,823 --> 00:16:33,823
It's no use, you tragic excuse for a nun. I'll crush you with the same powers that bewitch my audience.

304
00:16:33,823 --> 00:16:38,823
Poopy vampire, you think your performance is so great, you're in for a surprise!

305
00:16:38,823 --> 00:16:41,823
Kobito, wait! You can play when we're done!

306
00:16:49,823 --> 00:16:51,823
Kodaka, let's move. We're burning daylight.

307
00:16:51,823 --> 00:16:53,823
Okay, okay. I'm coming.

308
00:16:59,823 --> 00:17:02,823
Good afternoon. Look what the sun shined, Dragon.

309
00:17:02,823 --> 00:17:04,823
Great day for a sports festival, don't you think?

310
00:17:04,823 --> 00:17:06,823
You've all worked so hard.

311
00:17:06,823 --> 00:17:10,823
I hope you're as proud of yourselves as I am of the entire student body.

312
00:17:10,823 --> 00:17:13,823
I'm excited to see the results of all your efforts and talents.

313
00:17:13,823 --> 00:17:14,823
Nice.

314
00:17:14,823 --> 00:17:15,823
Parents, we are so happy to have you today.

315
00:17:15,823 --> 00:17:17,823
So our student body president is a girl.

316
00:17:17,823 --> 00:17:21,823
As always, thank you for your continued support for your children and our institution.

317
00:17:21,823 --> 00:17:23,823
This event represents...

318
00:17:23,823 --> 00:17:27,823
What now? I don't have anything to do until they're ready for me.

319
00:17:27,823 --> 00:17:28,823
Hey.

320
00:17:28,823 --> 00:17:29,823
Hey.

321
00:17:29,823 --> 00:17:30,823
Are you bored too?

322
00:17:31,823 --> 00:17:32,823
Yeah, I'm probably just gonna head home soon.

323
00:17:32,823 --> 00:17:33,823
Whoa, what? Why?

324
00:17:33,823 --> 00:17:34,823
Ugh, it's not a big deal. I should have just skipped.

325
00:17:34,823 --> 00:17:35,823
It's early and somebody already pissed me off.

326
00:17:35,823 --> 00:17:36,823
Who would that be?

327
00:17:36,823 --> 00:17:37,823
That skinny ponytail who spoke at the opening ceremony.

328
00:17:37,823 --> 00:17:38,823
No way. I had no idea you even knew the student body president.

329
00:17:38,823 --> 00:17:40,823
Well, we've never actually spoken. But I know enough to know that I hate her.

330
00:17:40,823 --> 00:17:41,823
Huh?

331
00:17:41,823 --> 00:17:43,823
Hinata Hideaka. She's a third year, and this is her second term as student body president,

332
00:17:43,823 --> 00:17:45,823
so that should tell you how ridiculously popular she is.

333
00:17:45,823 --> 00:17:48,823
She's smart and good at every sport imaginable. All the teams ask her to fill in for them.

334
00:17:48,823 --> 00:17:50,823
Even though she's busy, she'll make time for anything.

335
00:17:50,823 --> 00:17:53,823
But you're two minutes, and you are there for a reason?

336
00:17:53,823 --> 00:17:55,823
I mean, I am so I am and I am so happy.

337
00:17:55,823 --> 00:17:56,823
And what?

338
00:17:56,823 --> 00:17:57,823
You know, what are you going to do?

339
00:17:57,823 --> 00:17:58,823
I'm very close.

340
00:17:58,823 --> 00:17:59,823
What are you going to do now?

341
00:17:59,823 --> 00:18:00,823
What are you going to do now?

342
00:18:00,823 --> 00:18:01,823
How are you going to do now?

343
00:18:01,823 --> 00:18:02,823
How are you going to do now?

344
00:18:02,823 --> 00:18:04,103
How are you going to do now?

345
00:18:04,103 --> 00:18:05,823
I'm going to try not to do now.

346
00:18:05,823 --> 00:18:06,823
How are you going to do now?

347
00:18:06,823 --> 00:18:07,823
You are going to do now.

348
00:18:07,823 --> 00:18:12,043
fill in for them. Even though she's busy, she will make time for anyone who asks for a favor.

349
00:18:12,263 --> 00:18:16,763
Of course all the freshmen think she's like some kind of goddess. Yeah, why would anyone like

350
00:18:16,763 --> 00:18:21,843
someone like her? Well, it's not just that. It's because she's so not fake about it. I mean,

351
00:18:21,923 --> 00:18:25,983
Meet McNasty does all those sorts of things, but she does it to get people to worship her. She

352
00:18:25,983 --> 00:18:30,603
doesn't actually like anyone, you know? But Hinata is kind of like King Lear in a way.

353
00:18:31,263 --> 00:18:36,823
And what does that mean? It's a Shakespeare play, idiot. It's one of his most famous tragedies

354
00:18:36,823 --> 00:18:41,403
about an old evil king who causes his country nothing but misery until his own horrific death.

355
00:18:41,643 --> 00:18:46,323
Pretty much the entire cast dies in his wake. Uh, that's kind of a creepy comparison. I think

356
00:18:46,323 --> 00:18:50,203
it accurately represents my desire to see her suffer the same amount of pain she's caused me.

357
00:18:51,783 --> 00:18:56,923
She's making me want to puke just talking about her. I need to go to the nurse's office and lie down.

358
00:18:57,363 --> 00:19:00,103
So you're allergic to genuinely nice people. Got it.

359
00:19:00,103 --> 00:19:08,043
Rika? What the hell is she doing up there?

360
00:19:12,683 --> 00:19:14,963
Kodaka? The hell are you doing here?

361
00:19:15,183 --> 00:19:17,183
I was about to ask you the same thing.

362
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:19,643
Oh, um, Rika likes the feel of the wind.

363
00:19:20,503 --> 00:19:22,603
Well, you'll certainly get a lot of it dressed like that.

364
00:19:22,603 --> 00:19:26,703
Rika was feeling sporty today, so she decided to wear her gym outfit. What do you think?

365
00:19:26,703 --> 00:19:29,323
Yep, that's the right one. Why don't you go down and participate?

366
00:19:29,643 --> 00:19:33,763
Nah, Rika's got a lot of work left to do. Not that she would join in if she didn't.

367
00:19:33,843 --> 00:19:36,543
Holy crap. You stayed up all night working on the movie, didn't you?

368
00:19:36,563 --> 00:19:41,143
Oh, gross. Is it that obvious? Rika was totally going to wear her glasses today, but then she forgot.

369
00:19:42,863 --> 00:19:47,363
Something tells me I still would have known. Anyway, I hope you realize we appreciate you.

370
00:19:50,363 --> 00:19:53,903
Stop! Stop giving Rika genuine heartfelt compliments without notice!

371
00:19:53,903 --> 00:19:56,283
Her mind can't take it, and she's about to explode!

372
00:19:56,583 --> 00:19:57,823
Sorry, I take it back.

373
00:19:57,963 --> 00:20:00,463
Oh, yay! The race is about to start. Here they go!

374
00:20:03,843 --> 00:20:05,963
Look! Senna's already got a head start!

375
00:20:06,563 --> 00:20:09,123
Crap or duck! How does she run with those things?

376
00:20:10,563 --> 00:20:12,883
I don't know, but you seem pretty mad about it.

377
00:20:13,663 --> 00:20:17,643
No, Rika's just impressed with everything she can do on top of looking that way.

378
00:20:17,763 --> 00:20:18,843
Yep, she has a gift.

379
00:20:19,583 --> 00:20:23,023
What are your thoughts? Go ahead. Rika wants to know all the dirty details.

380
00:20:23,023 --> 00:20:26,903
There are no dirty details. She's just another club member, silly.

381
00:20:27,103 --> 00:20:28,343
She's also your betrothed.

382
00:20:29,003 --> 00:20:31,383
That's crazy, and it's not even happening anymore.

383
00:20:32,863 --> 00:20:35,943
Rika thinks that you might want to update Senna on that situation.

384
00:20:36,363 --> 00:20:37,883
Huh? Wait, what do you mean?

385
00:20:44,123 --> 00:20:47,003
Rika doesn't understand how you can complain that you're lonely

386
00:20:47,003 --> 00:20:48,983
when you don't let anyone get close to you.

387
00:20:48,983 --> 00:20:52,223
You pretend not to notice when someone is interested in your life.

388
00:20:53,023 --> 00:20:55,603
Then you make jokes so that no one will know when you're upset.

389
00:20:56,523 --> 00:20:58,183
Even though no one's given good reason,

390
00:20:58,303 --> 00:21:01,003
you convince yourself no one likes you so you never get hurt.

391
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:03,523
I get it. Is this what you want to tell Kobito?

392
00:21:03,763 --> 00:21:05,403
If so, go for it. It sounds good.

393
00:21:05,723 --> 00:21:06,903
That's not gonna work.

394
00:21:07,243 --> 00:21:09,303
Rika knows that you know the truth, but...

395
00:21:09,303 --> 00:21:13,803
She will continue to play the role you want her to play

396
00:21:13,803 --> 00:21:15,623
and protect your secrets so you're comfortable.

397
00:21:16,363 --> 00:21:17,783
But for how long, Kodaka?

398
00:21:19,383 --> 00:21:22,143
Rika predicts these games will get old after a little while.

399
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:23,243
What about...

400
00:21:23,243 --> 00:21:24,003
Shut up, Rika!

401
00:21:24,003 --> 00:21:24,083
Rika!

402
00:21:24,083 --> 00:21:32,783
I gotta go. Talk to you later.

403
00:21:36,663 --> 00:21:39,323
Kodaka, please always remember.

404
00:21:40,043 --> 00:21:43,003
Rika would bend over backwards for you anytime, anywhere.

405
00:21:45,523 --> 00:21:48,083
Huh? Sorry, I missed a lot of that.

406
00:21:48,083 --> 00:22:02,123
She would bend over backwards to help me anytime I needed it.

407
00:22:02,663 --> 00:22:04,683
The wind may have swallowed her words,

408
00:22:05,343 --> 00:22:09,183
but I've known the truth about how Rika feels for a very long time.

409
00:22:10,003 --> 00:22:10,363
So...

410
00:22:33,803 --> 00:22:34,243
You

411
00:23:41,636 --> 00:23:45,256
You played dumb, but my heart knew the truth all along.

412
00:23:45,276 --> 00:23:46,316
What? What?

413
00:23:46,496 --> 00:23:50,096
You denied when Rika cried, but she saw right through you. Yeah!

414
00:23:50,356 --> 00:23:51,316
What? What?

415
00:23:52,116 --> 00:23:55,356
You're not exactly singing the same song as Rika, are you?

416
00:23:55,496 --> 00:23:58,516
I'm sorry. I'll stop and try to collaborate and listen this time.

417
00:23:58,636 --> 00:23:59,236
What? What?

418
00:23:59,696 --> 00:24:01,916
Next time, dismay of I the chicken.

419
00:24:02,496 --> 00:24:03,996
Kodaka, will you marry Rika?

420
00:24:04,196 --> 00:24:06,576
No love games, turn our bad romance around!

421
00:24:06,876 --> 00:24:07,576
Um, no.

422
00:24:07,796 --> 00:24:09,056
Not even for the song?

423
00:24:10,836 --> 00:24:11,716
No love games, turn our bad romance around!

